1
00:00:19,650 --> 00:00:21,840
What happened?

2
00:00:21,840 --> 00:00:23,870
The baby-sitter called.

3
00:00:23,870 --> 00:00:26,360
His daughter is sick.

4
00:00:26,360 --> 00:00:27,990
What's wrong?

5
00:00:27,990 --> 00:00:32,290
I think she has a stomachache.

6
00:00:32,290 --> 00:00:37,070
He's a good father.

7
00:00:37,070 --> 00:00:41,120
So... what do you think of him?

8
00:00:41,120 --> 00:00:43,150
He's very nice.

9
00:00:43,150 --> 00:00:45,790
But I think he was nervous tonight.

10
00:00:45,790 --> 00:00:51,500
It was his first date in two years.

11
00:00:51,500 --> 00:00:53,440
Will you see him again?

12
00:00:53,440 --> 00:00:57,940
I hope so.

13
00:00:57,940 --> 00:01:01,890
This food is delicious.

14
00:01:01,890 --> 00:01:04,240
He didn't get a thing to eat.

15
00:01:04,240 --> 00:01:06,800
You ordered enough for three or four people,

16
00:01:06,800 --> 00:01:08,800
but I'm not complaining.

17
00:01:08,800 --> 00:01:12,510
The food is delicious.

18
00:01:12,510 --> 00:01:14,220
Who is that?

19
00:01:14,220 --> 00:01:15,730
Do you think it's...

20
00:01:15,730 --> 00:01:24,650
No. You won't believe it, Marilyn!

21
00:01:24,650 --> 00:01:29,900
I believe it. Even without looking.

22
00:01:29,900 --> 00:01:31,070
Hi!

23
00:01:31,070 --> 00:01:31,890
How...?

24
00:01:31,890 --> 00:01:35,030
Your downstairs neighbor let me in.

25
00:01:35,030 --> 00:01:36,100
Did you go home?

26
00:01:36,100 --> 00:01:37,640
I did , but everything is OK,

27
00:01:37,640 --> 00:01:40,440
so I decided to come back.

28
00:01:40,440 --> 00:01:42,930
To apologize for leaving so early,

29
00:01:42,930 --> 00:01:45,170
I brought you a little gift.

30
00:01:45,170 --> 00:01:45,890
It's a bonsai tree

31
00:01:45,890 --> 00:01:47,950
for your new apartment.

32
00:01:47,950 --> 00:01:50,170
Hi, Marilyn. I hope it's not too late.

33
00:01:50,170 --> 00:01:52,660
Oh, not at all. We're still eating.

34
00:01:52,660 --> 00:01:55,820
Please, come in. Join us.

35
00:01:55,820 --> 00:01:59,390
It's our meal from the restaurant.

36
00:01:59,390 --> 00:02:01,470
And how is your daughter?

37
00:02:01,470 --> 00:02:02,230
Oh, she's fine.

38
00:02:02,230 --> 00:02:04,240
It was only a tummy ache.

39
00:02:04,240 --> 00:02:06,350
It's good that you went back.

40
00:02:06,350 --> 00:02:09,780
Yes, I think it's important for me to be there

41
00:02:09,780 --> 00:02:11,570
since her mother died.

42
00:02:11,570 --> 00:02:16,260
I agree. Aren't you hungry?

43
00:02:16,260 --> 00:02:19,830
As a matter of fact... I am hungry.

44
00:02:19,830 --> 00:02:22,780
There's lots of food left.

45
00:02:22,780 --> 00:02:25,390
Mmm, this is delicious!

46
00:02:25,390 --> 00:02:26,830
Enjoy!

47
00:02:26,830 --> 00:02:28,960
I'm going to excuse myself.

48
00:02:28,960 --> 00:02:33,000
I have a lot of work to do to get ready for tomorrow.

49
00:02:33,000 --> 00:02:34,740
Good night, Harry. It was nice meeting you.

50
00:02:34,740 --> 00:02:35,970
Bye, Marilyn.

51
00:02:35,970 --> 00:02:37,250
Good night, Susan.

52
00:02:37,250 --> 00:02:40,700
Good night, Marilyn.

53
00:02:40,700 --> 00:02:43,790
She's going to a fashion show here in the city tomorrow.

54
00:02:43,790 --> 00:02:45,190
She is sleeping here

55
00:02:45,190 --> 00:02:48,200
so she won't have to travel from Riverdale in the morning.

56
00:02:48,200 --> 00:02:50,890
You two must be close.

57
00:02:50,890 --> 00:02:52,070
we are.

58
00:02:52,070 --> 00:02:55,400
The whole Stewart family is close.

59
00:02:55,400 --> 00:03:06,570
I like that.

60
00:03:06,570 --> 00:03:10,560
And then, two years ago, my wife died.

61
00:03:10,560 --> 00:03:12,990
You miss her.

62
00:03:12,990 --> 00:03:15,740
I do...yes, but I have Michelle...

63
00:03:15,740 --> 00:03:20,220
and with time...

64
00:03:20,220 --> 00:03:24,000
Is there anyone else in your life?

65
00:03:24,000 --> 00:03:29,550
No, not yet. What about you?

66
00:03:29,550 --> 00:03:31,600
Oh, I date occasionally,

67
00:03:31,600 --> 00:03:34,060
but my work keeps me busy.

68
00:03:34,060 --> 00:03:36,140
Ooh, speaking of keeping busy-

69
00:03:36,140 --> 00:03:37,560
I have an early start tomorrow,

70
00:03:37,560 --> 00:03:41,150
and the baby-sitter has to get home.

71
00:03:41,150 --> 00:03:42,980
Where did the time go?

72
00:03:42,980 --> 00:03:48,890
It's midnight.

73
00:03:48,890 --> 00:03:50,090
Thank you, Susan.

74
00:03:50,090 --> 00:03:52,700
I had a nice evening.

75
00:03:52,700 --> 00:04:02,160
Me, too, Harry.

76
00:04:02,160 --> 00:04:03,850
Harry?

77
00:04:03,850 --> 00:04:05,440
Yes?

78
00:04:05,440 --> 00:04:09,250
I'd like to meet your daughter someday.

79
00:04:09,250 --> 00:04:12,000
Does that mean that I can see you again?

80
00:04:12,000 --> 00:04:13,070
Of course.

81
00:04:13,070 --> 00:04:14,860
Wonderful. I'll call you,

82
00:04:14,860 --> 00:04:16,090
and we'll go out to dinner.

83
00:04:16,090 --> 00:04:16,780
Please do.

84
00:04:16,780 --> 00:04:19,080
I promise I won't leave early.

85
00:04:19,080 --> 00:04:22,180
It was for a good reason.

86
00:04:22,180 --> 00:04:24,290
You know something?

87
00:04:24,290 --> 00:04:25,270
What?

88
00:04:25,270 --> 00:04:28,810
I think we're going to be good friends.

89
00:04:28,810 --> 00:04:30,000
Good night, Susan.

90
00:04:30,000 --> 00:04:31,530
Good night, Harry,

91
00:04:31,530 --> 00:04:41,780
Have a safe trip home.

92
00:04:41,780 --> 00:04:44,270
Are you all right?

93
00:04:44,270 --> 00:04:46,310
Sorry.

94
00:04:46,310 --> 00:04:51,100
I never liked that umbrella stand.

95
00:04:51,100 --> 00:04:54,100
Good night, Harry.
